{
  "title": "Sever's Disease",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4074/severs-disease",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Oct 12 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Sever's Disease is a common idiopathic condition caused by overuse injury of the calcaneal apophysis in a growing child that presents with posterior heel pain.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with tenderness over the calcaneal apophysis with foot radiographs showing sclerosis and fragmentation of the calcaneal apophysis.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually activity modifications, stretching of the heel cord and NSAIDs as the condition typically resolves over time.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "commonly seen in immature athletes participating in running & jumping sports",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "frequently seen just before or during peak growth",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "exact etiology is unknown",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "thought to be due to traction apophysitis and repetitive microtrauma experienced during gait (similar to Osgood Schlatter's Disease)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The calcaneal apophysis experience significant force from combination of both",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "direct impact onto the heel during the heel strike phase of gait",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "opposing tension forces generated by the plantar fascia and the pull of the gastrocsoleus complex",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain in the area of the calcaneal apophysis in an immature athlete",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "pain increased with activity or impact",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "stretch of the triceps surae exacerbates heel pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "can display warmth, erythema, & swelling",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "tight Achilles tendon",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "positive squeeze test (pain with medial-lateral compression over the tuberosity of the calcaneus)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "pain over the calcaneal apophysis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "diagnosis is clinical as there is no established diagnostic criteria",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "sclerosis can be present in both patients with and without calcaneal apophysitis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "fragmentation is more frequently seen in patients with Sever's disease",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4074/images/sever.jpg",
                  "caption": "SEVER'S DZ"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "helpful to rule out other causes of heel pain (osteomyelitis, calcaneal bone cysts)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "can help localize inflammation to apophysis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "can rule out disorders of the body of the os calcis (stress fracture, lytic lesion, osteomyelitis)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Other",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "bone scan can show increase uptake at the apophysis, but is typically not helpful in diagnosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "symptomatic treatment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "modalities include",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "activity modification",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Achilles tendon stretches (can help decrease recurrence)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "ice application before and after athletic endeavors",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "use of heel cups or heel pads",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "NSAIDs",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "short leg cast immobilization of persistent pain",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "recurrence is common",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**there is no role for operative treatment**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Natural history",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**self-limiting entity** that resolves with maturation and the closure of the apophysis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
